---
title: "Provided Overlays"
---

Overlays are used to displaying messages over the top of the grid. The grid automatically displays an overlay when the grid state matches certain criteria.

The grid provides the following overlays:
- [Loading](#loading) - shown when data is loading
- [No Rows](#no-rows) - shown when there are no rows to display

## Loading

{% metaTag tags=["showLoadingOverlay"] /%}

The loading overlay is displayed when the grid property `loading` is set to `true` and takes precedence over other provided overlays.

{% apiDocumentation source="grid-options/properties.json" section="overlays" names=["loading"] /%}

 If the `loading` property is not provided, the grid automatically displays the loading overlay until both `rowData` and `columnDefs` are supplied with non-null values for the first time. This behaviour can be suppressed by setting `loading` to `false` before initialising the grid.

The example below shows the loading overlay when the `loading` property is set to `true`. Note how the loading overlays takes precedence over the no-rows overlay.

{% gridExampleRunner title="Loading overlay" name="loading-overlay"  exampleHeight=325 /%}

## No Rows

When `rowData` is set to an empty array `[]`, the grid automatically displays the no-rows overlay.

{% gridExampleRunner title="No Rows Overlay" name="no-rows-overlay"  exampleHeight=300 /%}

## Customisation

The provided overlays can be customised to change their content and appearance while still being triggered automatically by the grid. This is done via one of the following grid options: `overlayComponent`, `overlayComponentSelector` or via the `components` map.

{% note %}
Previously, the loading and no-rows overlays were customised via: `loadingOverlayComponent` / `loadingOverlayComponentParams` and `noRowsOverlayComponent` / `noRowsOverlayComponentParams`. These properties remain supported, for backwards compatibility, but are no longer recommended for use. See the [Documentation archive](/documentation-archive) for previous documentation.
{% /note %}

### Overlay Component

Provide a custom component to `overlayComponent` to be used in place of all the provided overlays. The custom component receives a `defaultOverlay` parameter which identifies which of the provided overlays will have been shown. This can be used to conditionally render different content based on the overlay type.

Custom parameters can also be supplied to the overlay component via the `overlayComponentParams` grid option.

{% apiDocumentation source="grid-options/properties.json" section="overlays" names=["overlayComponent", "overlayComponentParams"] /%}

```{% frameworkTransform=true %}
const gridOptions = {
    overlayComponent: CustomOverlay,
    overlayComponentParams: {
        myLoadingMessage: 'Custom loading message',
        myNoRowsMessage: 'Custom no rows message'
    },
};
```

### Overlay Component Selector

Dynamically provide different overlay components for each provided overlay type via `overlayComponentSelector`. The selector function receives a `defaultOverlay` parameter to identify the type of overlay required. Custom parameters can be supplied via the returned object's `params` property alongside the custom `component`.

Returning `undefined` from the selector function will cause the grid to fallback to the default provided overlay. This enables customisation of specific overlays while retaining the default behaviour for others.

The return type accepts component names as registered in the `components` map or component implementations.

{% apiDocumentation source="grid-options/properties.json" section="overlays" names=["overlayComponentSelector"] /%}

```{% frameworkTransform=true %}
const gridOptions = {
    overlayComponentSelector: (params) => {
        if (params.defaultOverlay === 'agLoadingOverlay') {
            return {
                component: CustomLoadingOverlay,
                params: {
                    loadingMessage: 'Please wait while data is loading...'
                }
            };
        }
        // return undefined to use the provided overlay for other overlay types
        return undefined;
    },
};
```

### Components Map

Overwrite the provided overlays by assigning a custom component to the matching key in the [`components` map](./components). Custom parameters can be supplied via the `overlayComponentParams` grid option.

```{% frameworkTransform=true %}
const gridOptions = {
    components: {
        agLoadingOverlay: CustomLoadingOverlay,
        agNoRowsOverlay: CustomNoRowsOverlay
    },
    overlayComponentParams: {
        loadingMessage: 'Please wait while data is loading...',
        noRowsMessage: 'No data available'
    }
};
```

{% apiDocumentation source="grid-options/properties.json" section="overlays" names=["components", "overlayComponentParams"] /%}

